WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.950 --> 00:00:04.103
- This is not who I normally am.

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:13.700
But this whole crisis
thing has changed me.

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:17.123
I'm a crisis nurse.

00:00:19.716 --> 00:00:21.854
Hey Craig, are you gonna keep fighting?

00:00:21.854 --> 00:00:23.040
- Yes.

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:26.493
- [Chelsea] I was in New York
from the time it started.

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:30.483
Now, I chase the outbreaks
throughout America.

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:36.220
I have to be on the road pretty much now.

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:39.180
15 minutes, that was a new record for me.

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:40.680
Time to get in the car and go.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:44.353
This is a long road.

00:00:46.590 --> 00:00:50.640
It doesn't matter if you're
liberal or you're conservative.

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:52.743
None of that matters to this virus.

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:55.184
It's impartial.

00:00:55.184 --> 00:00:58.017
(dramatic music)

00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:21.320
More and more nurses wanna speak out,

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:23.000
because only we're allowed
to see what goes on

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:24.880
inside these hospital walls.

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:26.939
(dramatic music)

00:01:26.939 --> 00:01:28.532
(alarm rings)

00:01:28.532 --> 00:01:31.949
- Second code of the day, this afternoon,

00:01:36.957 --> 00:01:40.407
and it's probably not
gonna be the only one.

00:01:40.407 --> 00:01:42.110
- [Chelsea] Traveling crisis nurse,

00:01:42.110 --> 00:01:44.713
pretty much we are called in last minute

00:01:44.713 --> 00:01:48.560
and are paid to help hospitals in any area

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:51.973
that needs help and is
struggling from COVID-19.

00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:55.990
You can see where the
next outbreak's happening

00:01:55.990 --> 00:01:58.710
by the amount of money
that they're paying.

00:01:58.710 --> 00:02:01.080
Every day the rates go up in the states

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:02.673
that are being hit the hardest.

00:02:02.673 --> 00:02:05.067
We're gonna go wherever
we're gonna get paid the most

00:02:05.067 --> 00:02:07.900
because our lives are on the line.

00:02:09.017 --> 00:02:12.423
We did not become nurses
to watch people die.

00:02:13.810 --> 00:02:15.453
We became nurses to stop it.

00:02:16.462 --> 00:02:17.740
(dramatic music)

00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:19.400
- It's going to be a rough night tonight.

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:20.930
We're about to lose another one.

00:02:20.930 --> 00:02:21.973
She's 43.

00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:26.503
We're intubating one right now.

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:29.750
And then we lost two today.

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:33.480
We'd appreciate your prayers right now.

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:34.313
Thanks guys.

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:37.650
- [Chelsea] We carry the
chance of being infected

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:40.043
and dying every day that we go to work.

00:02:41.209 --> 00:02:45.023
- I worked through the
pandemic in New York.

00:02:51.530 --> 00:02:55.293
And then I came to Texas to help.

00:02:56.887 --> 00:03:00.660
I just ask people to
please wear your mask.

00:03:02.630 --> 00:03:06.423
Even with all the precautions I took,

00:03:09.214 --> 00:03:10.403
I still got sick.

00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:15.630
- I was in New Jersey first,

00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:17.400
and then I went to New York City,

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:20.490
then Arizona, then Victoria, Texas,

00:03:20.490 --> 00:03:23.320
and now I'm in different part of Texas.

00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:25.050
Everything's gonna be okay.

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:27.258
Everything's gonna work out.

00:03:27.258 --> 00:03:28.950
It's gonna suck when I get there.

00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:31.810
How much do you wanna bet
it's going to be a cluster?

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:36.283
But, that's my job is to
help untangle those clusters.

00:03:38.660 --> 00:03:40.660
So I used to be Republican.

00:03:40.660 --> 00:03:43.443
I even voted for Trump.

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:46.970
I don't know what I am
politically anymore.

00:03:46.970 --> 00:03:50.110
I just wanna keep people
alive, that's my only goal.

00:03:50.110 --> 00:03:51.607
I work six days a week.

00:03:56.550 --> 00:03:59.483
I work from 7:00 AM to 7:00 PM.

00:04:05.380 --> 00:04:08.640
The vibe of the city is
they don't really believe

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:12.430
this virus is as big as we say it is,

00:04:12.430 --> 00:04:15.280
or as important as we say it is.

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:18.173
Things I've seen are
a lot of pool parties.

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:22.320
People walking around
without masks at all.

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:23.483
No social distancing.

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:30.110
I firmly believe as a Christian

00:04:30.110 --> 00:04:32.310
that simply wearing a mask

00:04:32.310 --> 00:04:36.000
and keeping your distance
from others is loving them.

00:04:37.795 --> 00:04:40.123
Okay, time to pray and go to work.

00:04:41.330 --> 00:04:44.927
I'm seeing overflows
of Coronavirus patients

00:04:44.927 --> 00:04:46.433
into other floors.

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:51.230
I'm seeing doors and
windows made out of plastic

00:04:51.230 --> 00:04:54.630
and plywood in hospitals,
which I've never seen before.

00:04:54.630 --> 00:04:58.453
I've seen little makeshift
COVID infection spaces.

00:04:59.660 --> 00:05:02.393
I've seen people get really sick.

00:05:03.420 --> 00:05:05.283
I see people die.

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:10.419
So I've seen a lot of
families in this town grieving

00:05:10.419 --> 00:05:15.419
and confused when I tell
them about the virus.

00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:18.937
I even had a patient
whose last words were,

00:05:18.937 --> 00:05:21.390
"I don't have the virus."

00:05:21.390 --> 00:05:22.503
And then he died.

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:26.993
Took about two or three
minutes before he was gone.

00:05:28.290 --> 00:05:29.503
Two or three minutes.

00:05:30.820 --> 00:05:34.600
When I talk to other nurses
about our mental health,

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:38.753
we all agree that we have PTSD.

00:05:39.810 --> 00:05:40.823
- I just can't.

00:05:45.250 --> 00:05:48.250
- [Chelsea] A lot of us
talk about panic attacks

00:05:48.250 --> 00:05:51.930
or nightmares, or reliving moments

00:05:51.930 --> 00:05:53.690
that we wish we didn't have to.

00:05:53.690 --> 00:05:55.010
- Can't wrap my brain around,

00:05:55.010 --> 00:05:57.643
not being there when my family's dying.

00:05:57.643 --> 00:05:59.810
It's tough to hear 'em

00:06:01.425 --> 00:06:03.970
saying good bye on a video.

00:06:03.970 --> 00:06:05.108
None of the news is good

00:06:05.108 --> 00:06:08.610
and I'm so burned out on
the families are accepting

00:06:08.610 --> 00:06:10.750
it's always, "Well he's a fighter.

00:06:10.750 --> 00:06:13.877
If anybody's going to beat
it he can, my dad can."

00:06:15.395 --> 00:06:16.900
It's just rough.

00:06:16.900 --> 00:06:21.093
- Still hoping I can make
it out there at one point

00:06:23.818 --> 00:06:26.318
And see my family that I miss.

00:06:28.680 --> 00:06:30.347
That I miss so much.

00:06:31.674 --> 00:06:34.091
I spent all day in this room.

00:06:36.623 --> 00:06:41.486
Nobody comes here except
for, you know, the nurses.

00:06:41.486 --> 00:06:43.403
It's been really tough.

00:06:49.940 --> 00:06:52.820
- So we just got off our shift.

00:06:52.820 --> 00:06:55.873
Talking about a patient
that is actively bleeding.

00:06:56.750 --> 00:07:00.990
That led into conversation
about this disease

00:07:00.990 --> 00:07:03.260
and how it causes blood clots.

00:07:03.260 --> 00:07:05.443
- When they go into what is called DIC

00:07:06.510 --> 00:07:08.860
and they start bleeding out everywhere,

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:11.873
we're kinda worried that's
what's gonna happen to his lady.

00:07:11.873 --> 00:07:14.540
(monitors beep)

00:07:23.666 --> 00:07:25.841
- [Chelsea] I have to
put one more tube in.

00:07:25.841 --> 00:07:27.840
Squeeze my hand.

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:30.350
Oh my God, oh my God.

00:07:30.350 --> 00:07:32.014
Like why is there so much blood.

00:07:32.014 --> 00:07:33.607
- [Woman] I don't know.

00:07:33.607 --> 00:07:34.880
- [Chelsea] She's DIC!

00:07:34.880 --> 00:07:36.528
She's gonna bleed out!

00:07:36.528 --> 00:07:38.522
She's a full code!

00:07:38.522 --> 00:07:40.022
She's a full code!

00:07:42.196 --> 00:07:45.029
(dramatic music)

00:07:50.920 --> 00:07:53.930
If this happens again, I'm
not gonna be a nurse anymore.

00:07:53.930 --> 00:07:56.030
I'm not doing this.

00:07:56.030 --> 00:07:56.990
I'm not dealing with this.

00:07:56.990 --> 00:07:58.240
Whatever that was just in the room with,

00:07:58.240 --> 00:07:59.373
I don't want that.

00:08:00.730 --> 00:08:02.313
I don't wanna die that way.

00:08:05.280 --> 00:08:07.523
My God, it was so bad.

00:08:10.560 --> 00:08:12.713
It was so horrifying to watch.

00:08:14.228 --> 00:08:16.328
I don't know why she was bleeding so much.

00:08:21.690 --> 00:08:23.240
I don't want whatever that was.

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:26.023
- I want everybody to know.

00:08:29.050 --> 00:08:31.287
How much I hate COVID

00:08:31.287 --> 00:08:34.520
and I hate people that think it's a hoax.

00:08:34.520 --> 00:08:35.760
Because you're not here

00:08:35.760 --> 00:08:38.150
and you're not taking
care of these families.

00:08:38.150 --> 00:08:40.320
And you're not holding
the hand of the dying.

00:08:40.320 --> 00:08:43.260
And you're not watchin'
somebody that can't breathe.

00:08:43.260 --> 00:08:46.030
And there's absolutely nothing you can do.

00:08:46.030 --> 00:08:51.030
So, up yours, if you're one
of those, just up yours.

00:08:53.810 --> 00:08:55.610
- I am going to get tested tomorrow.

00:08:56.670 --> 00:08:58.120
I have a really bad headache.

00:08:59.020 --> 00:09:02.153
I really hope I don't have
what I just saw today.

00:09:08.790 --> 00:09:10.080
- [Man] What's goin' on with you today?

00:09:10.080 --> 00:09:11.720
Are you sick?

00:09:11.720 --> 00:09:14.470
- [Chelsea] Have a headache and fatigue.

00:09:14.470 --> 00:09:16.363
I'm a COVID crisis nurse.

00:09:18.400 --> 00:09:20.943
I'm not the same person that I used to be.

00:09:21.860 --> 00:09:23.253
I miss who I used to be.

00:09:24.120 --> 00:09:27.460
Who I used to be is
better than who I am now.

00:09:27.460 --> 00:09:30.233
I still appreciate my life, trust me,

00:09:31.580 --> 00:09:33.580
that I know we're not promised tomorrow,

00:09:37.380 --> 00:09:39.163
but how did we get here?

00:09:41.950 --> 00:09:45.370
How did our country as a whole

00:09:46.340 --> 00:09:47.873
get to the place we're in now.

00:09:48.994 --> 00:09:51.827
(dramatic music)

